---
import '@fontsource/yuji-syuku';
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const title = 'Yoruyaki - July 2026';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} />
<main>
  <span class='date'>2026.07.25</span>
  <section>
    <h2>串焼き</h2>
    <div class='items'>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/shishitou'>
          <h3>しし唐</h3>
          <p>shishitou pepper, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/eringi'>
          <h3>エリンギ</h3>
          <p>king oyster mushroom, miso dengaku</p>
        </a>
      </div>
            <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/mune'>
          <h3>胸</h3>
          <p>breast, yuzu kosho/wasabi</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/negima'>
          <h3>ねぎま</h3>
          <p>thigh, scallion, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/obisori'>
          <h3>おびそり</h3>
          <p>inner thigh, oyster, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/hizanankotsu'>
          <h3>膝軟骨</h3>
          <p>cartilage, tare</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/sunagimo'>
          <h3>砂肝</h3>
          <p>gizzard, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
      <div class='item'>
        <a href='/skewers/hatsu'>
          <h3>ハツ</h3>
          <p>heart, sake, salt</p>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="notes">
    <h2>Notes</h2>
    <p>July was a busy month for us personally and so we wern't planning to do any events, however we saw that <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://sunflowersake.com/">Sunflower Sake</a> was going to be hosting a live watch party for the final day of the <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://www.instagram.com/sunflowersake/p/DbEHpPDFJGw">Nagoya Grand Sumo tournament</a>. The stream would start at 11:30pm which sounded like just the right time for some yakitori so I reached out to Nina & Molly to see if they'd be OK with me setting up the konro and grilling up skewers. Fortunately they were thinking the same thing!</p>
    <p>I didn't want to prep full chickens as I wasn't sure how many people would show up and I wouldn't have the space for the variety of skewers. I decided to do a smaller menu of just eight skewers without any sides to keep things simple. I picked up 20 thighs, 6 breast, two packs of heart, two packs of gizzard, two pounds of cartilage, six king oyster mushrooms, and 45 shishto peppers. I didn't use all the thigh, I kept some back to make karage at home the next day. I also didn't use the complete breast, just the top halves. I diced up the bottom half to use at home for dinner a couple days later. All in all I made 186 skewers. The first skewers came off at 11:30pm and the last came off around 1:30am, a few minutes later the tournament wrapped up. We didn't get a full count of everyone that came, but it was probably over 50 people, but not everyone had skewers. I only collected tips with no suggest amount and ended up getting around $2.50 per skewer.</p>
    <p>I ended up grilling 2-4 of the same types of skewer at a time and doing 2-3 types and then just putting them on plates in pairs for people to grab. I knew that if I took orders I wouldn't be able to keep track. I think it worked out OK, but if I do something like this again I'll probably change it. I think trying to fill the grill with 1-2 types at a time and then just placing them on a tray for people to take as they come off would work better. I was hoping to get thru the skewers quicker and trying to mix in too much variety slowed me down. I also lost 3-4 negima skewers as flare ups cause the skewers to burn.</p>
    <p>Overall it was a great time and really fit in with my image of how I want to serve skewers. Night time in an industrial area with some sake and other Japanese culture surrounding us and a good mix of Japanese and non-Japanese people. I was chatting after the event and said mentioned how I have no desire to serve skewers during the daytime under some pop up tent at whatever event. It's got to fit the feeling in my mind and heart.</p>
  </section>
</main>

<style>
  main {
    margin: 0 auto;
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 75ch;
  }
  .date {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    text-align: right;
  }
  section {
    margin-bottom: 4rem;
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 8fr;
  }
  .items {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    column-gap: 1rem;
    border-left: 1px solid rgb(173, 165, 159);
    padding-left: 2.2rem;
  }
  section h2 {
    font-family: 'Yuji Syuku', serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    writing-mode: vertical-lr;
  }
  section h3 {
    font-family: 'Yuji Syuku', serif;
    font-weight: 400;
    font-size: 1.6rem;
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  section a {
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .items > p {
    font-style: italic;
    grid-column-start: span 2;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
  p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
  .images {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    justify-items: center;
    padding: 0;
  }
  .images img {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 600px;
    height: auto;
  }

  .images iframe {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 600px;
    aspect-ratio: 9 / 16;
    border: none;
  }

  .notes {
    display: block;
  }

  .notes h2 {
    font-family: 'Noto Sans Variable', sans-serif;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0 0 1rem 0;
    font-size: 2rem;
    writing-mode: horizontal-tb;
  }

  .notes a {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .notes p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 650px) {
    .items {
      padding-left: 1rem;
    }
    p {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }
  }
</style>
